growth happens fast since we last talked  critter junction just bought another  gaming company  to enable cross-platform gaming now you  can raise virtual pets with friends on  pc  android and internet connected  calculators let's look at how critter  junction was able to quickly integrate  this new company's infrastructure into  their stack  when critter junction first bought the  new company there was one major concern  they had an entirely different cloud  provider and a different  architecture critter junction switched  over to containers and microservices  the new company's tech stack was a  monolith taking over the entire vm  critter junction uses a cloud native  approach the new company was hosting  everything on prem  critter junction really wanted to  acquire the new company to add its  cross-platform functionality to its own  offering  but everyone involved thought it would  take too much time and engineering  efforts to actually integrate  luckily critter junction called us  before they turned down this opportunity  to expand their offering  while still being able to scale and  manage diverse systems  we told them about google cloud's anthos  platform which lets you run apps  anywhere using gke  the idea is to provide a single platform  for managing  all kubernetes workloads wherever they  are  including on-prem and other clouds  this works because migrate from anthos  can turn vms and physical servers into a  kubernetes pod  which can run inside of a cluster just  like any other pod  once critter junction decided to go  ahead with this acquisition  they had a google cloud partner solution  team come  on site to help them set up a gke  on-prem cluster  and migrate over their newly acquired  company's existing infrastructure  next the team helped them set up a antho  service mesh  a fully managed service mesh to handle  communication between their on-prem  cluster  and their current gke cluster which  allowed the on-prem workload to be  visible  inside of 